# Taina reverse proxy + automatic TLS.
#
# This is the domain-set Caddyfile for a Compose deployment. For a box
# without a public domain, see Caddyfile.local instead: it serves any
# hostname with local-CA certificates issued on demand.
#
# TLS is coupled to your network topology (see guias/acesso-remoto.md). The site
# address below is {$TAINA_DOMAIN} with a default of :443:
#
#   - TAINA_DOMAIN set (e.g. taina.example.org) + ports 80/443 reachable:
#       Caddy issues a real Let's Encrypt certificate over HTTP-01 and adds the
#       HTTP->HTTPS redirect automatically. Recommended for a box with a public
#       domain.
#
#   - TAINA_DOMAIN empty (LAN only, or behind Tailscale/Headscale):
#       The address falls back to :443 and Caddy serves its own local-CA
#       certificate automatically (its internal issuer). Browsers warn until the
#       local root is trusted on each device. If you reach the box over
#       Tailscale/Headscale, prefer a real cert from the overlay
#       (`tailscale cert` / MagicDNS *.ts.net) and point clients at that name;
#       the overlay terminates TLS and this fallback is unused.
#
#   - DNS-01 (public domain behind NAT, or wildcard certs):
#       Requires a custom Caddy image built with your DNS provider module
#       (the stock caddy:2 image has no DNS modules). See the guide.
#
# Security headers (HSTS, nosniff, Referrer-Policy, frame-ancestors) are applied
# to every response.

{
	# Quieter logs for a home box; raise to INFO when debugging.
	log {
		level WARN
	}
}

{$TAINA_DOMAIN::443} {
	header {
		# HSTS: force HTTPS for a year, including subdomains. Browsers honor
		# this only over a trusted (non-self-signed) cert.
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
		# Disallow being framed by any other origin (clickjacking).
		Content-Security-Policy "frame-ancestors 'self'"
		# Do not advertise the server software.
		-Server
	}

	reverse_proxy taina:4000
}
